🐛 Bug Report: TechDocs page content is invisible after upgrading from 1.48.4 to 1.49.4 — Shadow DOM opacity remains 0

### 🔎 Search Terms

```plain
TechDocs opacity, TechDocs white screen, TechDocs blank, techdocs-react addon
```

### 🗃️ Project Area

Documentation

### 🔗 External Integration

AWS

### 📝 Description & Context

- After updating Backstage from version 1.48.4 to 1.49.4 and deploying to the dev environment, TechDocs page content became invisible.
- The sidebar, header, and search bar render normally, but the document content area stays completely blank.
- Inspecting the Shadow DOM with DevTools, the document HTML content is fully loaded (200 OK), but <html style="opacity: 0;"> is never updated to opacity: 1, and class="no-js" is never updated to class="js".
No JavaScript errors appear in the browser console.
- This was verified on both Chrome and Safari with the same result.
- The same TechDocs pages display correctly on our production environment running Backstage 1.48.4.

### 👍 Expected Behavior

- TechDocs pages should display document content as they did on Backstage 1.48.4.
- <html style="opacity: 0;"> inside the Shadow DOM should transition to opacity: 1.

👎 Actual Behavior with Screenshots
- The document content area is completely blank (white screen).
- No JavaScript errors in Safari console.
- Shadow DOM inspection shows the following:

```html
<div data-testid="techdocs-native-shadowroot">
  #shadow-root (open)
    <html lang="ja" class="no-js" style="opacity: 0;">
      <head>
        <title>My Project Documentation</title>
        <link rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://...assets/stylesheets/main.484c7ddc.min.css">
        ...
      </head>
      <body dir="ltr" style="--md-typeset-font-size: 16px;">
        <div class="md-container" data-md-component="container">
          <main class="md-main" data-md-component="main">...</main>
          <footer class="md-footer" style="width: 991px;">...</footer>
        </div>
      </body>
    </html>
</div>
```

### 🥾 Reproduction steps

1. Upgrade Backstage from 1.48.4 to 1.49.4 using yarn backstage-cli versions:bump
2. Build and deploy the application
3. Navigate to any TechDocs page (e.g., /docs/default/component/<entity-name>)
4. The sidebar and header render, but the document content area is blank
5. Open DevTools → Elements → find <div data-testid="techdocs-native-shadowroot"> → expand Shadow DOM
6. Observe that <html style="opacity: 0;"> never transitions to opacity: 1

We tested with the third-party Mermaid addon (backstage-plugin-techdocs-addon-mermaid) disabled by commenting out its import and JSX usage in source code. The issue persists. The remaining addons in use are all from @backstage/plugin-techdocs-module-addons-contrib (LightBox, TextSize, ExpandableNavigation, ReportIssue), but these have not yet been individually tested.

### 📃 Provide the context for the Bug.

Our current TechDocs implementation in `packages/app/src/App.tsx`:
```tsx
import { TechDocsIndexPage, TechDocsReaderPage, techdocsPlugin } from '@backstage/plugin-techdocs';
import {
  ExpandableNavigation,
  LightBox,
  ReportIssue,
  TextSize,
} from '@backstage/plugin-techdocs-module-addons-contrib';
import { TechDocsAddons } from '@backstage/plugin-techdocs-react';
// Mermaid addon disabled for troubleshooting — issue persists without it
// import { Mermaid } from 'backstage-plugin-techdocs-addon-mermaid';

// ...

<Route path="/docs" element={<TechDocsIndexPage initialFilter="starred" />} />
<Route path="/docs/:namespace/:kind/:name/*" element={<TechDocsReaderPage />}>
  <TechDocsAddons>
    <LightBox />
    <TextSize />
    <ExpandableNavigation />
    <ReportIssue />
    {/* Mermaid addon disabled for troubleshooting — issue persists without it
    <Mermaid config={{ theme: 'forest', themeVariables: { lineColor: '#000000' } }} />
    */}
  </TechDocsAddons>
</Route>
```

Our TechDocs implementation in `packages/app/src/components/catalog/EntityPage.tsx`:
```tsx
const techdocsContent = (
  <EntityTechdocsContent>
    <TechDocsAddons>
      <ReportIssue />
      {/* Mermaid addon disabled for troubleshooting — issue persists without it
      <Mermaid config={{ theme: 'base', darkMode: true, themeVariables: { textColor: '#bbbbbb' } }} />
      */}
    </TechDocsAddons>
  </EntityTechdocsContent>
);
```

TechDocs config (`app-config.yaml`):
```yaml
techdocs:
  builder: 'external'
  generator:
    runIn: 'local'
  publisher:
    type: 'awsS3'
    awsS3:
      bucketName: ${TECHDOCS_BUCKET}
      bucketRootPath: '/techdocs'
      region: 'ap-northeast-1'
  sanitizer:
    allowedIframeHosts:
      - drive.google.com
```

No changes were made to TechDocs routing, configuration, or addons between the working and broken environments. The version upgrade was performed using `yarn backstage-cli versions:bump`.

