Opt-in database-backed Starred Entities

### 🔎 Search Terms

```plain
star starred "starred entity" "starred entities"
```

### 🗃️ Project Area

Catalog

### 🔖 Need

The framework allows for the `StarredEntitiesApi` interface and `starredEntitiesApiRef` implementations to be swapped out. However, no persistence layer has ever shipped alongside it, leaving every team that outgrows `localStorage` to build their own solution independently.

We want stars to survive browser clears, incognito sessions, and machine switches. We also want a way to answer "which entities are most starred across the organization.

With a shared backend, this becomes a simple query. Teams can use it to understand which parts of the catalog are most valued, and to surface popular services in home pages or search rankings. And with the rise of skills in the world of AI, we want to surface the most starred skills for users to see what is popular.

### 📝 Proposal

Add an optional backend module and frontend module that replace the default localStorage-backed `StarredEntitiesApi` with a database-backed implementation. Teams that don't install the module get exactly what they have today. Teams that want persistence across browsers and sessions install two packages.

```tsx
// packages/backend/src/index.ts
backend.add(import('@backstage/plugin-catalog-backend-module-stars'));

// packages/app/src/App.tsx
import catalogModuleStars from '@backstage/plugin-catalog-module-stars';

createApp({
  features: [
    // ... existing features
    catalogModuleStars,
  ],
});
```

### Data Model

```
CREATE TABLE starred_entities (
  user_ref  TEXT NOT NULL,
  entity_ref TEXT NOT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (user_ref, entity_ref)
);
CREATE INDEX ON starred_entities (entity_ref);
```

### API surface

```ts
// exists todaay
interface StarredEntitiesApi {
  toggleStarred(entityRef: string): Promise<void>;
  starredEntitie$(): Observable<Set<string>>;
}

// new interface (represented separately for now
export interface CatalogStarsApi {
  getStarCount(entityRef: string): Promise<number>;
}
```

