NFS: useRouteRef in app root elements fails to resolve page routes before app finalization

### 🔎 Search Terms

```plain
"useRouteRef", "new frontend system", "nfs", "app root elements", "no path for routeref"
```

### 🗃️ Project Area

Core Framework

### 📝 Description & Context

In an app on the new frontend system, an `app/root.elements` extension that calls `useRouteRef` for a page route fails when it renders between sign-in and app finalization.

We are running into this with the announcements plugin:

```
Error in extension 'app-root-element:announcements/banner'; caused by Error: No path for routeRef{type=sub,id=announcements/view}
```

### 👍 Expected Behavior

Root elements that resolve page routes during bootstrap should get the correct route once the app is finalized.

